    pr_ref:  # fd15
    description: "**Parent.** `INV-fosab` (read-side sub-META: *Symbol-name lookup must disambiguate — kind-segregated registry OR calibrated-confidence multi-candidate emission*). This work is the kind-segregated-registry branch's shared-utility manifestation.\n\n**Closes.** `INV-paroh` (Verilog kind-blind dict — third sibling of the BUG-04 lineage; only open child of `INV-fosab`).\n\n## Decision background\n\n`WI-morud`'s description articulated an escalation rule: *\"If a third analogous bug surfaces in a third analyzer, escalate to a refactor that introduces a shared kind-segregated multi-value dict utility (cf. `inheritance.py:51-67`). Until then, per-analyzer targeted fixes are cheaper.\"*\n\nThe trigger has fired three+ times: three BUG-04-lineage analyzers (Rust `WI-milak`, VHDL `WI-morud`, Verilog `INV-paroh`) plus five cross-linker audit-cohort instances (subprocess_cli `WI-jifiv`, route_handler `WI-rusuh`, grpc `WI-patiz`, di_resolution `WI-fujum`, pyffi `WI-sifiz`). Eight known instances total — see `INV-fosab` for the catalogue.\n\nStakes analysis (recorded in INV-paroh discuss thread) concluded that future-instance prevention is the dominant expected-value driver: hypergumbo's spec anticipates additional analyzers (someday queue has 5+ language candidates plus dialect coverage gaps), and the per-instance cost of rediscovering and re-fixing the same bug compounds linearly in the number of future analyzers. Decision made 2026-05-17 to land Path B-thin.\n\n## Scope\n\n### Core deliverable (required)\n\nA small importable helper that replaces the silent-overwrite anti-pattern `dict[str, Symbol]` for name-keyed Symbol lookup:\n\n```python\n# Suggested location: packages/hypergumbo-core/src/hypergumbo_core/symbol_indexes.py\n\nclass SymbolByName:\n    \"\"\"Multi-value name → Symbol index with kind-aware lookup.\n\n    Use instead of ``dict[str, Symbol]`` for any analyzer or linker\n    that indexes Symbols by short name and might encounter collisions\n    across kinds or files. Lookup returns a list; callers apply\n    per-context preference cascades.\n\n    Pre-existing per-linker fixes for this anti-pattern under\n    INV-fosab — see message_queue, database_query, subprocess_cli,\n    di_resolution, pyffi for reference shapes.\n    \"\"\"\n    def add(self, sym: Symbol) -> None: ...\n\n    def lookup(self, name: str, *, prefer_kind: str | None = None) -> list[Symbol]:\n        \"\"\"Return all Symbols indexed under ``name``, optionally sorted by\n        ``prefer_kind`` first (i.e., trait > struct > enum when prefer_kind='trait').\"\"\"\n        ...\n\n    def lookup_one(self, name: str, *, prefer_kind: str | None = None) -> tuple[Symbol, bool]:\n        \"\"\"Return ``(symbol, is_fallback)``. ``is_fallback=True`` when\n        len(candidates) > 1, so callers can apply the ``INV-zuhub``\n        contract (confidence ≤ 0.5 + ``disambiguation_fallback=true`` flag).\"\"\"\n        ...\n```\n\nTarget footprint: ~20-30 LOC plus tests. Sized to be cheaper to import than to rewrite ad-hoc.\n\n### Apply to verilog (closes INV-paroh)\n\nReplace the single-value dict at `verilog.py:211` (insert) and `verilog.py:243` (lookup) with `SymbolByName`. Verify against `INV-paroh`'s acceptance criterion: a Verilog repo with two same-named symbols of different kinds (e.g., `module Foo` + a same-named package/primitive/interface) must resolve module-instantiation destinations to the module, not whichever was inserted last.\n\n### Optional follow-on (recommended stretch goal)\n\nRetrofit done audit-cohort sites whose existing shapes match the helper's API:\n\n- `subprocess_cli.py` `command_by_name: dict[str, list[Symbol]]` — matches the helper exactly\n- `inheritance.py:51-67` `class_by_name` / `interface_by_name` — matches the helper (two parallel instances)\n- `rust.py` BUG-04 fix per `WI-milak`\n- `vhdl.py` per `WI-morud`\n- `di_resolution`, `pyffi` — likely match\n\n**Stays bespoke (does NOT retrofit):** `route_handler.py`'s `_RailsIndex` (compound `(action, class_lower)` keys); `grpc.py`'s `servicer_by_name` (single-value by design) + `proto_service_by_name` (multi-value, but in a struct alongside other indexes). These shapes are genuinely beyond the helper's scope.\n\nIf the retrofit becomes larger than the helper itself, split into a separate follow-up PR.\n\n## Acceptance\n\n- `SymbolByName` helper exists with property tests covering: name collision across kinds, kind preference cascade, fallback detection on multi-candidate lookup.\n- Verilog `verilog.py:211,243` use `SymbolByName`; `INV-paroh`'s acceptance scenario passes.\n- All currently-passing tests continue to pass after any retrofit; coverage ≥ existing levels.\n- `INV-fosab` reaches `satisfied` once verilog work lands (its only open child closes).\n- The four audit-cohort sites that DON'T retrofit (route_handler, grpc, plus any others discovered) are documented in the helper module's docstring as out-of-scope-by-design, with a brief reason per site, so future readers don't try to \"complete\" the migration prematurely.\n\n## Out of scope\n\n- Path B-elaborate: a wrapper subsuming the compound-key or dual-shape cases (route_handler `_RailsIndex`, grpc dual indexes). Premature.\n- INV-zuhub contract enforcement audit of the 8 done sites (separate concern — could be a follow-up to verify per-linker fidelity, but not blocking).\n- Performance optimization. Multi-value lookup is still O(1) average; constant-factor delta vs single-value dicts is negligible at hypergumbo's scale.\n\n## Related\n\n- `INV-fosab` (parent META; this WI's existence respects WI-morud's escalation rule and gives INV-fosab its kind-segregated-registry-branch concrete artifact)\n- `INV-paroh` (closed by this WI's verilog work; isbefore link set)\n- `INV-zuhub` (edge-side fallback contract; the helper's `lookup_one` returns `is_fallback` so callers can apply this contract automatically)\n- `INV-dajaf` (super-META for symbol identity uncertainty; INV-fosab is its read-side child)"  # fd15
    fields: {}  # fd15
